@startuml ScriptureMemorizer
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 10
hide empty members

class Program {
  + Main() : void
}

class Scripture {
  - _scripture : List<Word>
  - _scriptureReference : Reference
  + Scripture(reference : Reference, text : string)
  + HideRandomWords(numberToHide : int) : void
  + IsCompletelyHidden() : bool
  + GetDisplayText() : string
}

class Reference {
  - _book : string
  - _chapter : int
  - _startVerse : int
  - _endVerse : int
  + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, startVerse : int)
  + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, startVerse : int, endVerse : int)
  + GetReference() : string
}

class Word {
  - _text : string
  - _isHidden : bool
  + Word(word : string)
  + HideWord() : void
  + Show() : void
  + IsHidden() : bool
  + GetDisplayText() : string
}

Program --> Scripture : creates and uses
Scripture "1" *--> "1" Reference : has
Scripture "1" *--> "*" Word : stores

note right of Program
  <b>Interaction:</b>
  1. Main builds a Reference, then passes it and the
     scripture text to new Scripture(reference, text).
  2. Loop: clear the console and print
     scripture.GetDisplayText().
  3. If scripture.IsCompletelyHidden() is true, the program ends.
  4. Otherwise prompt "Press Enter or type quit".
     Typing quit ends the program.
  5. On Enter, call scripture.HideRandomWords(3)
     and go back to step 2.
end note

note right of Scripture
  <b>Constructor:</b> splits the text string on spaces,
  creates a new Word for each piece, and adds it
  to _scripture. Program never sees the list.

  <b>GetDisplayText:</b> joins _scriptureReference.GetReference()
  with each word's GetDisplayText(), separated by spaces.

  <b>HideRandomWords:</b> uses Random to pick words that
  are still visible and calls HideWord() on each.

  <b>IsCompletelyHidden:</b> returns true only when
  IsHidden() is true for every Word.
end note

note bottom of Reference
  <b>GetReference:</b> returns "John 3:16" for a single
  verse, or "Proverbs 3:5-6" when an end verse was given.
  No prompting happens here; Program passes values in.
end note

note bottom of Word
  <b>Constructor:</b> saves the text and sets
  _isHidden = false (every word starts visible).

  <b>GetDisplayText:</b> returns _text, or underscores
  of the same length ("~_~_~_~_~_") when hidden.
end note
@enduml